--- (A) SU(2) single link: TWO different G'' on the SAME measure ---
   flat chart  G''_flat = -d2/da2 log rho_X        (H1 convention: includes Phi=-log J)
   Haar norm.  G''_Haar = -d2/da2 log(rho_X / J1)  (table convention: Jacobian divided out)
   beta=0.00  G''_flat =  0.820466709  (h=2e-2,1e-2,5e-3: 0.820473807,0.820464343,0.820461977)
             G''_Haar =  0.000e+00  (must be 0: pure/dressed Haar density is flat)
   beta=2.50  G''_flat =  1.346017812  (h=2e-2,1e-2,5e-3: 1.346021927,1.346016441,1.346015069)
             G''_Haar =  5.256e-01  (must be 0: pure/dressed Haar density is flat)
   anchor [T]: Haar Var(x3) = 0.929956045;  9/(4pi^2-6) = 0.268829910;  1/Var = 1.075319641
   anchor [T] (beta=0): Delta_dyn = 0 exact (S_W=0) and G''_flat = W_geo

--- (A2) Delta_dyn = E[H_vv] - Var(G_v)   (conditioned at X3=0, v=e3) ---
     H = d2_v S_W  (S_W only: the Jacobian Phi belongs to W_geo, not to Delta_dyn)
     at x3=0: G_v = d(S_W)/dr * (x3/r) = 0 exactly => Var(G)=Cov(G,Phi')=0
     H_vv(x3=0) = (dS_W/dr) / r   (radial derivative of a radial function)
   beta=0.00  Delta_dyn =  0.000000000   W_geo =  0.820461188   Delta_dyn+W_geo =  0.820461188
   beta=2.50  Delta_dyn =  0.589671194   W_geo =  0.756343417   Delta_dyn+W_geo =  1.346014612
\n--- (B) 2D YM  (spatial circle, constant holonomy coarse mode) ---
   [T] constant A1, A0=0  => every plaquette U_p = 1 exactly  => S_W == 0 along the whole line
       => G = d_v S_W == 0, H = d2_v S_W == 0 identically
       => Delta_dyn = E[H] - Var(G) = 0 exact;  X = -2Cov(G,Phi') = 0;  W_full = W_geo
   m = 3g^2/8 = 0.375000000  > 0   (Migdal: E_j = (g^2/2) C2(j), C2(1/2)=3/4)  [T]*
   H1 convention  (flat chart, includes Phi):  G'' = W_geo =  0.820466709  > 0
   table convention (Haar-normalized, no Phi): G'' =  0.000e+00  == 0   <-- the table's value
   => the table's '2D YM: G'' = 0' is NOT the same functional as H1's G''
   => in H1's own convention, G'' = Delta_dyn + W_full = 0 + 0.820467 > 0
   => Delta_0^2 = Delta_dyn / a^2 = 0 exactly (EQUALITY, not negative / imaginary)

--- (C) M6 = harmonic(x) (x) free(b):  G'' = 2w, Delta_dyn = 2w, m = 0 ---
   [T] identity G'' = 4(E0 - V(0)) = 4(w/2 - 0) = 2w = 2.000000   (identical marginal rho ~ exp(-w a^2))
   W_full = 0 (Lebesgue measure, Phi == 0)  =>  Delta_dyn = 2w = 2.000000
   [T] along the free direction b: S == 0 => G == H == 0 => Delta_dyn(b) = 0
   spectrum on a circle of length L: E(n,k) = w(n+1/2) + (2 pi k/L)^2/2
        L  m_L = min(w, (2pi/L)^2/2)
        8                0.308425138
       16                0.077106284
       32                0.019276571
       64                0.004819143
      256                0.000301196
     1024                0.000018825
   => m = 0 in the limit; and the inf over coarse modes of Delta_dyn is min(2w, 0) = 0

--- (D) free massless field:  S == 0, Phi == 0 ---
   G'' = 0, Delta_dyn = 0, W_full = 0, m = 0   (exact; acid test passes with equality)

